// A `Login` response that logs `input.user` as a `Long` is rejected at ingestion; alice's later
// `Read` is recorded before her own `Login` response. The specification stamps the `Read` one tick
// after the response, and allows it; the crate takes the times as given, and denies. The harness
// reports the decision once, as stamping, not also as a decision ingestion changes.
@id("read_after_login")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::response{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
